Package: whispaste
Version: __VERSION__
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Silvio Lindstedt <silvio-lindstedt@outlook.com>
Homepage: https://whispaste.de/
Depends: libgtk-3-0, libsecret-1-0, libnotify4, libayatana-appindicator3-1, libasound2, libcurl4, libkeybinder-3.0-0, liblzma5, libc6, zlib1g
Description: Voice-input tool — hotkey, speak, paste anywhere
 WhisPaste is a voice-input tool. Press a global hotkey, speak, and the
 transcribed text is pasted at the cursor position of whatever application
 you are currently typing in — system-wide, not bound to a single app.
 .
 Transcription runs locally on your device via whisper.cpp or Parakeet, or,
 optionally, through a cloud provider you choose. The speech engines run
 inside the app process. The speech model is downloaded once, when you start
 the model download during setup, into the user's writable config dir
 ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/whispaste, default ~/.config/whispaste); audio never
 leaves your device in local mode.
 .
 The package installs a udev rule that gives the logged-in user access to
 /dev/uinput, which automatic pasting needs.
